title ALES60 — Lotus's downward expander: the compressor mirrored under the threshold
prompt recur the 1024-round itinerary Lindy-first crux-first, take the next agent-doable Lotus lap, send each finished increment, stop at custody gates
think The ALES59 log closed the held dynamics arc (attack/hold/release for limiter, compressor, gate) and named the next Lindy-first cruxes: the lookahead delay line (a Keaton's-word horizon — needs a check-in) or a fresh dynamics gesture (de-esser, sidechain, expander) — each a clean rung on the proven follower with no custody gate. Crux-first among the self-approvable three: the expander, because it completes the classic dynamics QUARTET and is the one rung that makes the family symmetric about the threshold.
think The dynamics family sits in two mirror-pairs about the threshold. Above: compressor (ALES50, divides the excess) and its infinite-ratio limit the limiter (ALES49, pins the peak). Below: the gate (ALES51, floors the quiet) already exists, yet its SOFT member was missing — the true downward mirror of the compressor. That soft member is the downward expander.
think The gate and the expander are genuinely different rungs, not the same law twice. The gate divides the WHOLE below-threshold magnitude by the ratio, so it STEPS at the threshold (a sample just below jumps to ~thr/ratio). The expander keeps the threshold whole and widens only the DEFICIT: m<thr -> new_m = thr - (thr-m)*num/den, floored at 0. That is continuous at the threshold (deficit 0 -> new_m = thr, the identity), the exact mirror of the compressor's thr + (m-thr)*den/num.
think Proved the algebraic laws before coding: unit ratio (num=den) gives new_m = thr-(thr-m) = m, identity everywhere; num/den>=1 gives widened deficit >= deficit so new_m <= m (reduces, never boosts); a ratio far past the deficit drives new_m negative, floored to 0 — the gate reached from within, mirroring how the limiter is reached from within the compressor.
think Overflow bound: deficit <= sample_max (32767), num a u32, product <= ~1.4e14, inside i64; new_m may go negative before the floor so it is clamped to 0 then narrowed to i16 where 0<=new_m<=m<=sample_max fits. One compare, one multiply, one divide per sample; nothing on the audio path overflows.
think Built lotus/expand.rye on gate.rye's exact frame — same ExpandError faults (BadThreshold/BadRatio/BadRange), same edge checks before any write, opening triad, >=2 asserts per fn each with a positive // invariant:, the one changed line the gain law. Witness tools/ales_expand_witness.rish mirrors the gate witness and re-proves ALES50 the compressor GREEN so the mirror-pair rests side by side.
obs GREEN on the first build; the gate/compressor idiom carried over clean. tame_style_check bans clean, expand.rye carries asserts (not on the zero-assert ratchet). Purely local — no lookahead, socket, network, keys, funds, device, or sample rate; every custody gate untouched. The dynamics family is now symmetric about the threshold: compressor above, expander below.
